{{/*
  APPROVED — ticket 13, variant A (the danger zone), with the ?return= path folded in.
  This is the markup to build; it is NOT wired into the app. The prototype that
  produced it (three variants behind ?variant= on the real edit page) has been deleted.

  Sits in templates/edit.html, AFTER the closing </form> of the edit form.
  It MUST be a sibling form, never nested: edit.html is already one
  <form method="POST" action="/expenses/edit/{id}">, and a nested <form> is invalid HTML.

  Chosen over:
    B — a server-rendered confirmation page showing the expense being destroyed.
    C — a trash icon in the title row with a CSS-only <details> reveal.
  Both were zero-JS, which turned out to buy nothing: the edit page already mounts the
  category-pills and description-pills islands (handlers_html.go:367), so it requires JS
  regardless. Ticket 08's JS-free property belongs to the daily view, not to this page.

  Known cost, accepted: confirm() states the expense ID and nothing else. It cannot show
  the amount, the description, or the date. The guard is only as good as "#49".

  See .plan/daily-timeline/tickets/13-delete-affordance-home.md
*/}}

<div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
  <div class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 mb-2">
    Danger zone
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      Deleting an expense is permanent. It cannot be undone.
    </p>

    {{/* Sibling form. Separate action, separate method target, never nested. */}}
    <form
      method="POST"
      action="/expenses/delete/{{.Expense.ID}}"
      onsubmit="return confirm('Delete expense #{{.Expense.ID}}?')"
    >
      {{/* The return path, server-issued. HandleEdit reads ?return= off the URL that
           brought the user here (the ledger row's Edit link carries it) and passes it
           through. HandleDelete validates it as a local path before redirecting:
           must begin with "/", must not begin with "//", must not contain a scheme.
           Falls back to "/" when absent or rejected. */}}
      <input type="hidden" name="return" value="{{.ReturnTo}}" />

      <button
        type="submit"
        class="bg-red-50 text-red-600 hover:bg-red-100 rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium shrink-0"
      >
        Delete expense
      </button>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
